      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Developing the structural diversity of microporous zeolitic frameworks with integrated semiconducting properties is promising but remains a challenge. Reported here are two unique crystalline semiconductor zeolite analogues constructed from two kinds of indium selenide clusters with augmented ctn and zeolite-type sod networks. The intrinsic semiconducting nature in these In-Se domains gives rise to pore-size-dependent and visible-light-driven photocatalytic activity for organic dye degradation."},
